================================================================================
64-state Boolean reading
  T1, T2sep, T2adj are sums of exact q[M] over 64 Boolean missed-sector atoms.
  The quotient preserves cyclic adjacency of the missed sectors and destroys:
    speed ownership, relation height, and the x-location of the atoms.
  Challenged assumption: vertices need not be runners or arcs; here the useful
    vertices are low-depth Boolean atom types, i.e. missed-sector shapes.
  What is proved here is finite bounded-bank separation modulo AP dilation,
    not a global LRC14 cap theorem.

